<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE lm8a-hainan-2026-11-20 ascent (3DOF sim)</name><description>RETIMED 2026-11-18: NET moved from 2026-11-20T11:00:00Z to 2026-11-20T11:59:00Z (Fri 20 Nov 3:59 a.m. PST). LL2 id a2975167-7c6f-4403-99e1-b40df17c8140, status Go (was TBC), window 11:51-12:17Z, last_updated 2026-11-18T08:29:42Z. NOTAM RPHI B5829/26 re-checked: same South China Sea polygon, still daily 1100-1400Z on 20-23 Nov, which covers 11:51-12:17Z. Azimuth stays 142.99 deg (mean bearing to the B5829/26 and B5830/26 centroids). HYDROPAC 3352/26 was not the azimuth used on the previous file (its areas bear 140.17/140.30/140.30 deg) and no newer hazard notice replacing those polygons was found. utc shifted by +3540 s; ECEF geometry unchanged. ILLUSTRATIVE.
ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Long March 8A Y13 (SatNet LEO Group TBD?, Hainan Commercial LC-1) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Method: first-principles 3DOF sim (/workspace/trajectory-deck/sim/ascent3dof.py): WGS-84 rotating Earth, J2, US76 drag,
thrust SL/vac interpolated on ambient pressure, mdot from Isp, staging/fairing/coast events; vertical rise to 17.0 s (rule: config guidance),
pitch kick 4.779 deg over 10 s, gravity turn, linear-tangent upper-stage steering tan(theta)=0.5795-0.001431*(t-t_ign), solved by optimizer.
Vehicle config: Long March 8A (sim/vehicles/lm8a.json; every number carries a source URL, derivation, or ASSUMPTION).
LM-8A: thrusts/Isp/GLOW from Wikipedia; stage masses DERIVED from LM-8 vs core-only GLOW differences plus ASSUMED propellant fractions.
ILLUSTRATIVE. PRE-FLIGHT. Long March 8A Y13, SatNet LEO Group TBD?, Hainan Commercial Launch Site LC-1. LL2 id a2975167-7c6f-4403-99e1-b40df17c8140, status To Be Confirmed, NET 2026-11-20T11:00:00Z (Fri 20 Nov 3:00 a.m. PST), window 11:00-14:00Z, orbit LEO with no altitude (net precision Hour). LL2 pad name Commercial LC-1, 19.597275N 110.930753E.
Vehicle and stage data reused unchanged from vehicles/lm8a.json, the lm8a-wenchang (SatNet LEO Group 28, 25 Oct 2026) baseline. Energy-cutoff mode: no published LM-8A ignition/cutoff/separation sequence, so this is not timeline mode. Thrusts/Isp/GLOW from Wikipedia; stage masses DERIVED with ASSUMED propellant fractions; fairing 1500 kg ASSUMED; 3 s pre-S2 coast ASSUMED; Cd 0.667 transferred from the LM-3B fit (aero only). Guidance (vertical rise until 60 m/s, 10 s kick) is the vehicle-file ASSUMPTION.
TARGET ASSUMED: 700 km circular, borrowed from the Group 28 config. Not this flight&#x27;s published orbit. Azimuth 142.99 deg is the mean bearing to the NOTAM RPHI B5829/26 and B5830/26 fall-area centroids (142.920 and 143.061 deg). HYDROPAC 3352/26 was not used for the azimuth. No deploy time is published.
Target (see launch config): insertion 700 km, apoapsis 700 km, fpa 0, launch azimuth 142.99 deg; payload 5000 kg.
Pad: 19.597275N 110.930753E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s (Earth-relative).
T0 used: 2026-11-20T11:59:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.
POST-CUTOFF: deploy time unpublished (No payload-deploy time is published. LL2 gives the mission as a batch of 9 LEO communications satellites and does not give a separation time; CASC/CALT have not published one for this flight. The Group 28 config likewise had no deploy time. Propagated 2 revs on the inferred insertion orbit.). From insertion T+764.0 s the stage is propagated for TWO revolutions (osculating period 98.77 min) on the inferred insertion orbit (same WGS-84/J2/US76-drag model); rows tagged -coast/-burn.
POST-CUTOFF end T+12617 s: inferred insertion orbit, +2 revs (deploy time unpublished): alt 699.98 km, osculating 699.8 x 700.2 km, i 56.356 deg.
POST-CUTOFF note: Upper-stage residual venting after cutoff is not modelled.</description>
